---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  description="About Fret Canvas: a visual fretboard tool for scales, chord tones, tuning workflows, and export-ready diagrams."
  title="About | Fret Canvas"
>
  <div class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-[56rem] flex-1 pt-14">
    <article class="w-full pb-8">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[color:var(--md-sys-color-on-surface)] md:text-5xl">
        About Fret Canvas
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-[46rem] text-base leading-8 text-[color:var(--md-sys-color-on-surface-variant)]">
        Fret Canvas lets you visualize notes on the fretboard interactively from chords and scales.
        You can also click directly on the fretboard to add or remove notes manually.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6 text-base leading-8 text-[color:var(--md-sys-color-on-surface-variant)]">
        I used to use an iPad to hand-draw chord and scale notes on fretboard diagrams to practice. It worked but was a bit cumbersome, and it was awkward to keep drawing while holding the instrument. Fret Canvas was built to make that
        process faster and easier to handle directly in the browser.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-6 text-base leading-8 text-[color:var(--md-sys-color-on-surface-variant)]">
        You can select an area of the fretboard image and export it as an image file.
      </p>

      <section class="mt-12 border-t border-[color:var(--md-sys-color-outline-variant)]/70 pt-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-[color:var(--md-sys-color-on-surface)]">Q&amp;A</h2>

        <div class="mt-6 space-y-8">
          <section>
            <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-[color:var(--md-sys-color-on-surface)]">
              Can I use exported images on my own website or in videos?
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-8 text-[color:var(--md-sys-color-on-surface-variant)]">
              Yes. Feel free to use them anywhere. No need to ask first.<br />
              Credit is not required, but it would be appreciated.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section>
            <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-[color:var(--md-sys-color-on-surface)]">
              Does it support bass or other string instruments?
            </h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-8 text-[color:var(--md-sys-color-on-surface-variant)]">
              Yes. It supports bass and other string instruments. You can change the number of strings and the tuning from the <span class="font-medium">Tuning</span>
              menu.
            </p>
          </section>
        </div>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
